{
  "version": 1,
  "claim": "hp-sim5 at c2450975 has a set of new, reproducible incorrect behaviors: (1) the USD loader ignores xformOpOrder for translation and ignores metersPerUnit, so shipped wheel prims are 0.20-3.09 m from compliant USD and a valid millimetre scene loads 1000x too large; (2) a missing optional spool attribute silently deletes a motor and leaves dangling cable joints that throw on the first step; (3) the RRF host build loses one microstep around a standstill (M400), changing a later 1 mm move from 80 to 79 steps and leaving -1/+1 steps after an exact return; (4) legal multi-driver CAN configs lose 100% of commanded motion and become 8.34 mm of phantom extrusion; (5) the default Klipper MCU upload player drops the first queue_step batch of every stepper except the first (shipped draw_squares.txt: B -4.052 vs -5 steps; 0.0409 mm effector offset); (6) a single non-finite input coordinate silently NaNs the whole cable network while reporting 0 N; (7) applying a baked scene plan depends on the ambient enableLayering flag (1.804 rad, 7.2 cm). Each case has a one-command reproducer that exits nonzero with the stated numbers.",
  "scope": "Simulation and firmware-emulation evidence on revision c2450975 with the bundled native addon and checked-in Wasm module, shipped HP3/HP4/HP5/slideprinter/cubecorners assets and the prebuilt RRF simulator. No hardware validation.",
  "limitations": [
    "No hardware validation; all evidence is simulation or firmware emulation.",
    "The USD op-order case is an asset/loader contract defect: simulator geometry matches author intent while a compliant USD consumer sees different geometry.",
    "Findings 4 (multi-driver CAN) and 7 (ambient flag) are not reachable from bundled machines or the shipped UI.",
    "The Klipper player loss is one-time per stream (constant position bias), not accumulating, and does not affect RRF preset buttons.",
    "The physics NaN cases require invalid or opt-in-latent inputs.",
    "Wasm ran inside Node V8, not a browser; one host, one Node build."
  ],
